#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""h2h.py - 10-25 (the user: "Go on the Maya head-to-head, but build and run it only after the round's last measurement, so
the build doesn't disturb any timing. Follow the plan as written: review first, offline build with unshare -rn, our pinned
llama.cpp copy, three engines. For quality, add Strata's scoring function to the local Maya build so all three engines are
checked with the same KL method"). The plan: results/ds41/maya-catchup.md (item 2); the review: security-review.md here.
User unit ds41-h2h; resumes from results/ds41/h2h/state.json. H2H_DRY=1: print the plan and write the configs only.
  0. wait until the tuning round has finished cleanly (ds41-tune inactive 3 checks in a row, tune.log "round finished
     after" and "8080 back on P021m"); a round that stopped otherwise: one alert, then keep waiting (nothing starts)
  1. gap: port_gap4.sh begin in its own scope (queue held, test lock, 8080 stopped), LDR + SearXNG 8889/8890 stopped,
     drive-temperature log on
  1b. pinpoint (10-26, the user: "yes, report only. Run it after the last end test and before the Maya head-to-head"):
     skipcheck.py pin - the ship config built up from the final check's base one change at a time, teacher-forced, on
     the round's engine; which change moves the KL percentiles most -> results/ds41/tuning/pinpoint.md (feeds IQ_Q8K)
  2. source: `git archive v1.1.28` of the reviewed clone -> ext/maya-v1.1.28-src (+ maya-score.patch: Strata's score());
     our llama.cpp (strata/third_party/llama.cpp, 3cf03257, clean) copied -> ext/llama.cpp-3cf03257, pin checked
  3. build under `unshare -rn`, nice 19: the review's configure flags, `--target maya-ds4` only
  4. pack under `unshare -rn`: pack_gguf.py (python -I, cwd outside the tree) --out ext/maya-pack-ds41, the 4 IQ2_XXS
     shards + the Engram file; ds4.txt must say 6 experts per token
  5. configs: S = the round's ship config (state "final") on the round's engine; M1 = Maya with Strata's arithmetic; M2 =
     Maya's defaults minus anything lossy or not repeatable (PCIe lane off). Strata-only settings are not carried
     (DS4_SETTLE_MS: Maya has no settle); --ssd-cache N -> DS4_WARM_CAP_GB N (both engines start with up to N GB of hot
     experts in RAM). Effort: the integer 62 for every arm (Strata renders it byte-identical to "medium", checked 10-25)
  6. speed: S1 M1 S2 M2 S3, full protocol (3 passes; maya-speed3.py for all); Maya arms inside maya-netns.sh (server,
     engine, client, guards on the namespace's own 127.0.0.1, no network)
  7. follow-ups: maya-ckpt_client.py on M1 and M2 (Jan's format; S = the round's ckpt end test on the same engine)
  8. KL: M1 and M2 scored by the patched maya-ds4 and judged exactly as the round's final check (skipcheck "final":
     against teacher/final-base with final-R1-chunk4096 / final-R2-cpu-share as rounding references; S = final-cand-final)
  9. results/ds41/h2h/summary.md; port_gap4 end (P021m back); services back; alert
Kernel rule: any kernel event or failed kernel check stops here with 8080 left stopped and an alert (stricter than the
page-allocation-failure drop rule: this run has no triage of its own). Memory: tunearm's guards (12 GB hard, 15 soft,
swap guard v2); a "failed: memory" arm is recorded and the next one runs.
"""
